<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Augustin Calmet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1672–1757</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Dom Augustin Calmet, Antoine Augustin Calmet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Augustin Calmet was a French Benedictine monk and scholar from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, abbot of Senones from 1728. He wrote a vast literal commentary on the Bible, a dictionary of the Bible and a history of Lorraine, and his treatise on apparitions and vampires of 1746 made him widely known. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voltaire">Voltaire</a> and other writers visited him at Senones to use its library.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/augustin-calmet.jpg" alt="Augustin Calmet" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rijksmuseum · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_van_de_theoloog_Augustin_Calmet,_RP-P-1883-A-7537.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
